========================================================================
5. Built-in data, certificates and layouts
========================================================================

- W3C and W3C Credentials Community Group JSON-LD context documents built into
  core (w3c/ld/LdContexts.kt) - W3C Software and Document License
- Country signing CA certificates (core BuiltInCscas) taken from the German
  CSCA master list published by the Federal Office for Information Security
  (BSI), checked against BSI's published self-signed root; public certificates
  of the issuing states, no change other than selection
- Built-in trust anchors (core/.../trust/BuiltInAnchors.kt,
  BuiltInPublicRoots.kt, BuiltInTestAnchors.kt) are public certificates
  published by their certification authorities and by the Multipaz project;
  they are reproduced for certificate path validation only. The same holds
  for the certificates tools/trust-roots keeps in its pinned files (downloaded
  from each CA's own site), for the partner CA certificates in
  tools/trust-roots/esign-partners (taken from the certificate bundle the
  e-sign platform esign.cn publishes for its partner CAs), and for the public
  service certificates in test-servers/src/test/resources/chains.
- Public trust lists: the Adobe Approved Trust List and the EU trusted lists
  (ETSI TS 119 612, published by the European Commission and the member
  states) are downloaded and verified by the application at run time; only
  SHA-256 fingerprints of their signing certificates are built in.
- The offline OpenCerts layouts (core/.../opencerts/OpenCertOffline.kt)
  follow the templates of the OpenCerts demo renderer
  (demo-renderer.opencerts.io, GovTech Singapore); they were written anew and
  contain no logos or pictures from it.
- The JBIG2 decoder (core/.../document/image/Jbig2.kt) was written following
  ITU-T T.88 and the structure of the JBIG2 decoder in pdf.js (Mozilla
  Foundation, Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js).

